+# Quantitative parameter system
+
+This build exposes the authored numeric world/runtime surface as URL parameters and as an in-game viewer/editor opened with **P**.
+
+## Coverage
+
+- `main.js`: 5,427 authored numeric literals outside final CONFIG leaves, including numeric CONFIG object keys.
+- `player-physics.js`: 80 numeric literals.
+- `city-performance.js`: 81 numeric literals.
+- `vendor/city-pack/asset-catalog.js`: 3,740 numeric placement/model metadata values.
+- `CONFIG`: 417 numeric leaves, registered **after seeded randomization and ?city/?citySize handling**, so the panel shows the actual effective values for the current world.
+
+Total cataloged quantitative knobs: **9,745**, plus the current seed control in the editor header.
+
+Deliberately excluded: Three.js/addon implementation internals, GLB binary data, the large noise/public-data corpora, and the parameter editor's own UI-layout constants. Those are dependencies/data/tool chrome, not authored city/runtime tuning.
+
+## Query syntax
+
+Semantic CONFIG values use readable keys:
+
+```text
+?cfg.movement.speed=5.2
+?cfg.camera.fov=92
+?cfg.maze.cols=101&cfg.maze.rows=101
+```
+
+Source literals use stable content/context hashes:
+
+```text
+?n.physics.ed10b2c866cd=0.0002
+?n.main.84dad655289e=4
+?n.assets.313b9890731b=9
+```
+
+The hash is intentionally not a sequential index. Unrelated insertions elsewhere in the source therefore do not renumber every saved parameter URL. If the local source context actually changes, an old key is more likely to become unknown than to silently control the wrong numeric literal.
+
+Current literal schema: `cf4ad1f9a6ad0a6e`.
+
+## P parameter viewer/editor
+
+Press **P** after the world loads. The heavy ~2 MB source metadata catalog is lazy-imported only then; normal startup never downloads/parses it.
+
+The panel starts with the values that are actually active in this exact load. It has:
+
+- searchable key/function/source context,
+- CONFIG / main / physics / performance / asset-catalog filters,
+- active value vs desired value,
+- live/reload mode,
+- overridden-only filtering,
+- reset per value / reset visible,
+- editable seed,
+- Copy URL,
+- **GO / RELOAD**.
+
+GO keeps ordinary non-parameter query flags, serializes only desired numeric overrides, and pins the current seed by default so all untouched seeded/randomized CONFIG values reproduce the current world's tuning.
+
+### Runtime modes
+
+**LIVE WORLD**: explicit binding to current state. Current bindings include movement speed/sprint, touch/look controls, desktop pointer speed, camera FOV/near plane, active draw distance/light budget/pixel ratio/bloom, runtime fog/ambient gradient intensity, sun intensity/color/position, and hemisphere color.
+
+**LIVE/FUTURE**: a numeric literal occurs inside a runtime function. Its generated module-local backing variable is changed immediately, so future executions use the new number. Existing state that consumed the value earlier is not magically reconstructed; GO is still the authoritative rebuild.
+
+**RELOAD**: a top-level/module initialization or generation-only value. It is staged for GO and does not partially mutate already-built geometry.
+
+## Dangerous values are intentionally allowed
+
+The parser accepts normal decimal/scientific notation, hex (`0xff00aa`), `Infinity`, `-Infinity`, and explicit `NaN`. The parameter layer does not add safety clamps around values that the original code did not clamp. This is a lab/debug surface and can absolutely produce impossible geometry, broken physics, absurd memory use, or a failed boot.
+
+## Parameterized-load diagnostics
+
+`index.html` detects numeric parameters before `main.js` starts fetching and prints a `PARAMETERIZED LOAD` line in the visible boot log.
+
+After module initialization and final CONFIG override application, `main.js` logs the schema/counts and a table of requested/applied values. The same information remains available via:
+
+```js
+window.__params.schema
+window.__params.counts()
+window.__params.state('cfg.movement.speed')
+window.__params.report()
+window.__params.desired()
+window.__params.set('cfg.movement.speed', '5.2')
+window.__params.reloadUrl(12345)
+```
+
+## Performance design
+
+The parameterization deliberately does **not** perform URL/map lookups in hot loops. Each authored literal resolves once into a plain module-local variable at module initialization. Runtime-editable literals use a generated setter only when the P panel edits one.
+
+The 9,328-row source metadata catalog is not in the normal module graph; `parameter-editor.js` imports it only on the first P press. The enlarged city-pack catalog is still ordinary static data after its one-time numeric resolution.
